{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And when you reap</b> — qere in it ובקצירכם, that one must leave one [part] from the סמ\"ך (which is the measure of pe'ah). And four times the language of קציר in the verse, to exclude: קצרוהו לסטים — bandits harvested it; כרסמוהו נמלים — ants gnawed it; שברתו הרוח — the wind broke it; אכלתו בהמה — an animal ate it." "<b>The corner of your field</b> — in gematria (the measure of) pe'ah: one out of sixty." "<b>shall be cut off</b> — and adjacent to it: ובקצרכם. One who robs the poor and designates their designations — נפש, a soul."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:00.366740441Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}